\9-- want to reconcile without matching against the existing set. This has the\
\9-- effect of all current children being unmounted; even if the type and key\
\9-- are the same, the old child is unmounted and a new child is created.\
\9--\
\9-- To do this, we're going to go through the reconcile algorithm twice. In\
\9-- the first pass, we schedule a deletion for all the current children by\
\9-- passing nil.\
\9workInProgress.child =\
\9\9reconcileChildFibers(workInProgress, current.child, nil, renderLanes)\
\9-- In the second pass, we mount the new children. The trick here is that we\
\9-- pass nil in place of where we usually pass the current child set. This has\
\9-- the effect of remounting all children regardless of whether their\
\9-- identities match.\
\9workInProgress.child =\
\9\9reconcileChildFibers(workInProgress, nil, nextChildren, renderLanes)\
