\9-- Is it safe for this component to read from this source during the current render?\
\9local isSafeToReadFromSource = false\
\
\9-- Check the version first.\
\9-- If this render has already been started with a specific version,\
\9-- we can use it alone to determine if we can safely read from the source.\
\9local currentRenderVersion = getWorkInProgressVersion(source)\
\9if currentRenderVersion ~= nil then\
\9\9-- It's safe to read if the store hasn't been mutated since the last time\
\9\9-- we read something.\
\9\9isSafeToReadFromSource = currentRenderVersion == version_\
\9else\
\9\9-- If there's no version, then this is the first time we've read from the\
\9\9-- source during the current render pass, so we need to do a bit more work.\
\9\9-- What we need to determine is if there are any hooks that already\
\9\9-- subscribed to the source, and if so, whether there are any pending\
\9\9-- mutations that haven't been synchronized yet.\
\9\9--\
\9\9-- If there are no pending mutations, then `root.mutableReadLanes` will be\
\9\9-- empty, and we know we can safely read.\
\9\9--\
\9\9-- If there *are* pending mutations, we may still be able to safely read\
\9\9-- if the currently rendering lanes are inclusive of the pending mutation\
\9\9-- lanes, since that guarantees that the value we're about to read from\
\9\9-- the source is consistent with the values that we read during the most\
\9\9-- recent mutation.\
\9\9isSafeToReadFromSource = isSubsetOfLanes(renderLanes, root.mutableReadLanes)\
\
\9\9if isSafeToReadFromSource then\
\9\9\9-- If it's safe to read from this source during the current render,\
\9\9\9-- store the version in case other components read from it.\
\9\9\9-- A changed version number will local those components know to throw and restart the render.\
\9\9\9setWorkInProgressVersion(source, version_)\
\9\9end\
\9end\
\
\9if isSafeToReadFromSource then\
\9\9local snapshot = getSnapshot(source._source)\
