\9\9-- // we made it larger, a product metric in www regressed, suggesting there's\
\9\9-- // a user interaction that's being starved by a series of synchronous\
\9\9-- // updates. If that theory is correct, the proper solution is to fix the\
\9\9-- // starvation. However, this scenario supports the idea that expiration\
\9\9-- // times are an important safeguard when starvation does happen.\
